Archive(live).blob bytes  157; sha256 2c840501b3eea39a...
tarfile backed by         io.BytesIO(self.blob) (Archive.__init__ lines 451-453)
   (reference file deleted from disk)
arc.member() after delete b'REAL-RELEASE-BYTESREAL' len=144
-> still the release bytes: True
   => after Archive() is constructed the file on disk is NEVER read again:
      arc.member() serves io.BytesIO(self.blob); the digest check at line 921
      hashes arc.blob, not the file. Deleting/overwriting the file is inert.

Q2c  ordering in the frozen counter (line numbers from the frozen file)
   915: apath = os.path.join(S, "counter-archive.tar.gz")
   920: arc = Archive(apath)  # one read: the bytes hashed are the bytes parsed
   921: if hashlib.sha256(arc.blob).hexdigest() != ARCHIVE_SHA:
   936: legs = bind_one(tree, os.path.join(tree, path), S, f"b{n}", vocab, arc, detail)
   => the counter downloads, reads into memory and hashes its reference BEFORE
      the first replay is launched (bind_one -> start_replay). There is no
      window in which a replay can change the bytes that are compared.
